userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Two hydrogen atoms have a potential energy minimum at a specific separation (74 pm) where nuclear–electron attraction and nucleus–nucleus repulsion balance — that separation is the covalent bond length.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A covalent bond has a definite length because energy rises in both directions from the minimum — closer costs repulsion, farther costs lost attraction — so 74 pm is the one separation where the two effects balance.
DEMO STEPS: 5 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

